<title>USA: Pulitzer November revenues rise 22.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer November revenues rise 22.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pulitzer Publishing Co said Thursday that revenues for the four weeks ended December 1 rose 22.1 percent, to $48.9 million from $40.0 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>It said year-to-date revenues advanced 14.5 percent, to $489.5 million from $427.7 million.</p>
<p>Revenues include Scripps League Newspapers Inc, which was acquired on July 1, 1996. Scripps added $6.1 million in the month and $29.1 million in the year to date, Pulitzer said.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
